#version 460
// d4r engine, preset M: the stage after the network. Expands the last decoder's tokens (64 channels, FP8) to 17
// values per render pixel (one matrix product per 4x4-token block) and turns them into the reconstruction's
// per-pixel inputs: a recurrent four-channel feature blended with its reprojected history, three gate values,
// three softmax weights and a 2x2 covariance. See M_NOTES.md.
// DOT2: the same stage for GPUs without cooperative matrices or FP8 (RDNA2): the product on v_dot2_f32_f16 with the
// same binary16 rounding after every 32 products, FP8 in integer arithmetic (fp8_soft.glsl); binding 8 holds the
// matrix widened to binary16 pairs [32][80] by the runtime. A workgroup is four of the blocks (2x2), so the product
// runs with a token per lane and wave-uniform weights.
// INT8 (with DOT2, D4RM0007): the product on v_dot4_i32_i8 instead: every token's 64 channels as int8 with one scale
// (its largest magnitude / 127), binding 8 the matrix as int8 [16][80] words and 80 column scales (runtime_m.inc
// widenM), the sums in f32 without the binary16 roundings. Steam Deck 720p 547 -> 450 us, the final image within the
// run-to-run spread of the binary16 product.
